WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:05.520
Guided by self-styled "sharp-eyed promoter" Gallagher, 
we entered the underground duel venue.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.320
It was a place for illegal duel gambling.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:15.200
Kurosaki was already there, 
looking for strong duelists,

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.360
and taking the #1 slot in popularity and power.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:25.990
Gallagher wanted us to fight Kurosaki, 
to put on a big show for everyone.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.510
And if we win ten straight underground duels,

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:33.000
we can enter the duel festival 
known as the Friendship Cup.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.380
And so, I challenged Kurosaki to a duel.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:37.080
Pendulum Summon!

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:40.350
Come to me, my monsters!

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:45.790
Pendulum Summon?

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:49.050
Yes, in the underground duel venue, 
in City's central region.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:51.340
Send someone to monitor the situation at once.

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:54.180
They may be hiding there.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.160
I'll take care of it.

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:01.530
D-Wheels.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:05.790
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:07.500
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.940
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:13.130
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:51.280
Underground Riding Duel!!

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:54.360
Three monsters at once?

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.760
And without tributing a monster of Level 5 or above?

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:01.680
Well? Shocked are you?

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.360
This was the main reason that 
Dennis here caught my eye.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.330
Come to think of it, that Central Park 
duel we saw on TV also...

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:11.360
That's right. He used it then, too!

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:12.390
Was that it?

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:17.910
That's right! The summoning method that's like 
magic would make any man lose his nerve.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:22.780
Its name... Pendulum Summon!

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:28.990
This is the sight of sights that I, 
the sharp-eyed promoter Gallagher,

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:33.660
have prepared for you today!

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:41.030
Now, now. You haven't seen anything yet.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:44.270
I activate the effect of Wing Sandwichman.

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:47.470
When I have two Wing Sandwichmans on the field,

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:49.980
I can set the card between them to Level 5.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.960
Wing Sandwichman's effect

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:01.510
has given him three Level 5 
cards on the field at once?

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:10.600
I overlay my two Level 5 Wing 
Sandwichmans and Ball Balancer!

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:15.870
Descend, performer of the demon world!

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.470
Xyz Summon!

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:21.910
Rank 5 Performage Shadow Maker!

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:26.670
Well? What do you think of that?

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:32.910
Pendulum Summon, into Xyz Summon!

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.630
I've captured the spectators' hearts.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.520
I really am amazing!

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:43.200
If Kurosaki takes that hit, he's lost.

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:46.190
I don't want Kurosaki to lose.

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:48.970
But Dennis is great, too!

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:54.560
If #1 Kurosaki loses to someone 
who only started today,

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.370
he'll end up deep in the hole...

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.430
Well, what happens next?

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:01.080
Can Kurosaki protect his #1 slot?

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:03.830
Or will we see the birth of a new #1?

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.810
Kurosaki or Dennis?

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:10.060
Dennis or Kurosaki?!

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:14.670
Sorry, but I'll be taking your #1 slot.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:22.830
You're the one who will lose.

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:31.540
Are they about to get malicious?

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:34.010
Battle!

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:37.320
Shadow Maker! Attack Blaze Falcon!

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:47.450
Equip Spell Raptor's Ultimate Mace's effect activates!

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:52.560
When the monster it's equipped to is destroyed, 
damage to me is reduced to 0,

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:56.980
and I can add one Rank-Up-Magic 
from my deck to my hand.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:01.770
I add Rank-Up-Magic Revolution Force!

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:07.600
Such pointless struggling...

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:12.220
Even if you add Quick-Play Spells to your hand, 
you can't use them during my turn.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:15.820
You have no monsters on your 
side of the field. You've lost.

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:18.390
I activate my trap card Lightning Quick.

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:23.800
Its effect lets me activate Quick-Play 
Spells in my hand.

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:30.400
I activate my Quick-Play Spell Rank-Up-Magic 
Revolution Force!

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:34.650
I take control of an Xyz Monster 
on your side of the field!

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:45.800
And I raise it to a Raidraptor of the next rank!

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:55.960
Proud falcon, flap your wings that are 
stained with the blood of heroes

00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:58.340
and travel the path of revolution.

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:01.430
Rank Up Xyz Change!

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:07.840
Appear, Rank 6 Raidraptor — Revolution Falcon!

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:12.800
There are no monsters left on 
Dennis's side of the field.

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:14.880
The tide has completely turned.

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:18.170
Bravo... Bravo!

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:23.420
It's an exciting back and forth, 
worthy of a battle for #1!

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:32.900
I-Impossible!

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:35.110
What's going on?

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:42.470
I thought Shadow Maker was a component 
for Revolution Falcon's Rank Up...

00:07:42.470 --> 00:07:48.840
When Shadow Maker is targeted by 
effects, I can use one Overlay Unit

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:53.670
to Special Summon another Shadow 
Maker from my Extra Deck.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:57.760
A card that can continuously 
make shadows of itself?

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:04.060
All units, report in.

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:06.670
Unit 2, in place.

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:09.200
Units 3, 4, 5, in place.

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:12.700
Areas C and D are sealed off.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:15.370
What about the Tops?

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:18.110
Three minutes until they're evacuated.

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:23.210
All right, we'll execute in three minutes.

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:26.710
Now, let's make this show even more exciting!

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:48.110
Wh-What? A power outage?

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:50.410
This is security!

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:54.450
You are all under arrest for illegally 
gambling on riding duels!

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:57.660
Stay right where you are! Do not resist!

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:03.820
I repeat. You are all under arrest for 
illegally gambling on riding duels!

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:10.730
Hey, wait!

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:16.950
You got me.

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:22.000
We've taken the Commons in the audience thought 
to be dangerous elements into custody.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:26.970
The two who use Xyz Summon and 
Pendulum Summon, and their comrade.

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:30.330
Excellent work.

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:32.480
Continue expanding the search area.

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:36.200
Search every corner of that Commons 
underground duel venue.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:41.140
The fugitives are likely taking shelter 
among the Commons.

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:45.290
Arrest anyone who resists, by any means necessary.

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:46.420
Roger!

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:50.740
Perfect.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:53.780
Now, I can accomplish my cleanup of City.

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:57.410
Synchro Summon!

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:01.350
You can't do that. That isn't a Tuner Monster.

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:02.850
You got me...

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:05.050
Don't say that!

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:08.840
Sorry, sorry. Let's try again!

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:09.450
Brother, where are you?

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:15.530
Hey... Have you seen Serena and Sawatari?

00:10:15.530 --> 00:10:18.600
That scary girl and the stuck-up guy?

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:21.000
Haven't seen 'em. They aren't inside?

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:23.560
No, I can't find them anywhere.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:27.530
I guess they're still at the City center.

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:31.880
I'm sure they couldn't have gone up there, but...

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:34.780
What am I gonna do with them?

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:39.600
Layra, what's wrong?

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:41.590
I'm going to find my brother!

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:42.550
No!

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:48.490
S-Sorry. I'm not angry with you.

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:50.600
Brother...

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:55.540
Right now, it's dangerous for 
us to walk around in City.

00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:57.620
Crow told us that.

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:01.160
For now, let's wait. Okay, Layra?

00:11:02.210 --> 00:11:06.500
Don't worry... I promise I'll get 
you back to Reiji Akaba.

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:12.750
I attack directly with Lunalight Cat Dancer!

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:26.030
Brilliant.

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:28.390
That's the eighth one.

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:34.560
For someone who said she was looking for 
Yuzu, you're pretty focused on dueling.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:36.040
What about Yuzu?

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:39.330
Of course looking for Yuzu is important.

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:42.780
But finding strong duelists is also important.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:49.250
Tell me! Who's the strongest person around?

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:52.420
H-Him...

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:58.650
Jack Atlas? I've seen these posters around...

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:00.740
How can I fight him?

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:05.970
Target located. She's the Fusion 
Summoner from the other day.

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:08.210
She's with the blond.

00:12:08.210 --> 00:12:11.020
Then, track them both.

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:14.560
Wherever they go, we're sure to find

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:17.700
the other user of Pendulum Summon.

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:25.490
Those two went out on their own again?

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:30.380
Darn it, I told them not to go!

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:33.460
Sorry, I'll warn them when they get back.

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:40.340
I bought the stuff you asked for...

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:42.910
What, you're still here?

00:12:43.250 --> 00:12:45.000
Aren't you...

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:46.620
My friend, Shinji.

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:49.010
Thanks for before.

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:51.560
You guys are wanted, you know.

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:53.690
You'd better not get the kids drawn into it.

00:12:53.690 --> 00:12:55.610
I'll be careful.

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:58.220
Shinji, you came!

00:12:58.220 --> 00:12:59.920
Shinji!

00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:02.890
I brought some good stuff.

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:06.490
What is this stuff?

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:07.950
Did you steal it?

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:09.230
Great work!

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:12.920
S-Stupid! It was on sale for cheap!

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:16.780
What's with those expressions? It's true!

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:20.120
Just eat it already.

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:23.950
You, too. There's plenty, so help yourself.

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:29.150
Helpful provisions from our fellow Commons. 
Eat them and be grateful.

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:31.440
Well, I'm off.

00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:33.460
Sure. Thanks.

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:37.860
Be careful. Security's still searching 
the city everywhere for you.

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:39.470
Sure, got it.

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:40.490
Bye!

00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:41.460
See you later!

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:52.140
Delicious!

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:53.980
Hey, come join us.

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:58.810
If you don't hurry, it'll all be eaten.

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:01.290
Hurry it up.

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:05.900
What? Still hesitating?

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:10.900
No need to hesitate. Just come eat.

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:14.090
Is that an order?

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:18.050
Order?

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:22.600
You've been here three days, and that's 
the first thing you say to me?

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:25.380
Okay, you want an order, huh?

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:30.450
Before you eat, wash your hands properly.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:36.550
Hey! You guys wash up, too!

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:38.440
Kinda late for that!

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:40.420
We're already eating!

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:43.580
No complaints... It's an order.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:45.130
Okay.

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:53.690
Why is he so timid about everything?

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.290
I don't really know, either.

00:14:57.720 --> 00:15:03.280
Kids should be free, doing what they want.

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:06.280
If they mess up, give a hint for improvement.

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:10.250
I want...

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:15.730
I want to bring back his smile.

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:18.920
And not just Layra's.

00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:22.670
I want everyone in the world 
to smile and be happy.

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:27.660
If you want people to be happy, 
you need to fill their bellies first.

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:30.510
You don't get it at all.

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:33.210
Smiles are the symbols of happiness!

00:15:33.590 --> 00:15:35.680
Can smiles fill their bellies?

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:39.360
No matter how much you eat, it isn't happiness 
without a reason to smile.

00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:40.990
That's just sad.

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:44.460
You have to fill those bellies first! 
Smiles come second!

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:45.920
That isn't true!

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:49.370
Sorry, but your way of thought 
is a sign of your blessed life.

00:15:49.370 --> 00:15:50.750
What was that?

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:53.160
Everyone knows having a full belly isn't enough!

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:57.580
Wrong! You need to fill someone up first. 
That's the most important thing!

00:15:57.580 --> 00:15:58.900
That isn't true!

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:03.590
Hey, you guys. You're happier 
with full bellies, right?

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:08.250
Come on, speak up... Layra, what do you think?

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:12.580
It's actually all about smiles, right, Layra?

00:16:12.890 --> 00:16:14.330
Getting full comes first!

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:15.290
Smiles!

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:16.960
A belly full of food!

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:17.950
Smiles!

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:18.640
Food!

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:19.620
Smiles!

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:22.170
You're one ignorant fool...

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:23.360
No, you are!

00:16:23.360 --> 00:16:26.190
Okay, let's settle who's right with a duel!

00:16:26.190 --> 00:16:27.720
Bring it on.

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:30.800
I'll show you the entertainment duels 
that my father pioneered!

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:39.240
He must be pretty famous...

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:41.590
I hope it isn't just talk.

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:49.080
The farther into the center, 
the stricter the security.

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:53.190
What can you do? I'm hungry, 
so let's head back for now.

00:16:56.860 --> 00:17:01.830
I'm going to teach you how important 
a full belly is, you stubborn fool!

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:05.070
I'll make you see that a smile 
is the most important thing!

00:17:05.070 --> 00:17:06.040
Food!

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:07.000
Smiles!

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:09.740
Those guys are hopeless.

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:11.120
It's so silly.

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:13.080
They're so immature.

00:17:13.080 --> 00:17:14.120
Duel!

00:17:15.280 --> 00:17:17.540
Field Spell Crossover!

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:28.360
I'll take the first move!

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:31.060
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:33.400
Does he mean us?

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:35.520
Indeed, I do.

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:41.870
Using Pendulum Summon, I'll give you an 
eyeful of my magnificent monsters!

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:43.340
Pendulum Summon!

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:45.910
Hurry! Hurry!

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:49.010
And when I win brilliantly, 
I'd like a round of applause!

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:51.220
He's trying to finish me, right off the bat?

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:55.840
I set the Pendulum Scale with 
Scale 1 Stargazer Magician

00:17:55.840 --> 00:18:00.470
and Scale 8 Timegazer Magician!

00:18:10.170 --> 00:18:14.970
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 2 and 7 simultaneously!

00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:16.040
Wow!

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:17.580
Hurry up!

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:20.540
Swing, my soul's pendulum.

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:23.510
Draw an arc of light in the sky!

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:25.250
Pendulum Summon!

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:27.860
Come out, my monsters.

00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:33.460
First, Performapal Silver Claw!

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:36.930
Then Performapal Salutiger!

00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:41.900
And finally, Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:44.370
Wow!

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:45.970
Three, at once!

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:48.040
Cool!

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:52.220
My Pendulum Summon has caused 
the flower known as a smile

00:18:52.220 --> 00:18:54.520
to blossom on those three children's faces!

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:56.380
Cool!

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:03.320
You're making an awful lot 
out of a slightly good reception.

00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:05.950
I now end my turn!

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:08.430
That's the end of the first act.

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:12.650
What, a duel?

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:15.870
While I was gone, they started 
doing something interesting.

00:19:16.270 --> 00:19:19.100
Let's go! Start the hungry duel!

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:21.000
My turn!

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:22.910
When there are no cards on my field,

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:27.460
I can Special Summon Blackwing — 
Gust the Backblast from my hand!

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:34.560
And when Blackwing is on my side of the field,

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:37.680
I can Special Summon this card!

00:19:37.680 --> 00:19:41.230
Come out, Blackwing — Oroshi the Squall!

00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:47.260
Crow got two monsters out, just like that!

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:50.000
I tribute Oroshi the Squall,

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:54.120
to Tribute Summon Assault Blackwing — 
Kunai the Drizzle!

00:19:54.970 --> 00:20:00.360
It's possible to summon more than one 
monster without Pendulum Summon.

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:02.980
I guess we both had a good debut.

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:07.580
If you use Pendulum, I'll use Synchro Summon!

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:11.960
But you don't have a Tuner Monster 
on your side of the field!

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:14.400
Don't underestimate the Blackwings.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:16.830
I activate Kunai the Drizzle's effect!

00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:22.830
When this card is Tribute Summoned with a 
Blackwing, it can be used as a Tuner Monster.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:28.460
Level 5 Kunai the Drizzle tunes 
Level 2 Gust the Backblast!

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:34.360
Spread your ebony wings,

00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:37.930
and strike the ground with the speed of lightning!

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:40.680
Synchro Summon!

00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:45.420
Rain down, Assault Blackwing — 
Raikiri the Rain Shower!

00:20:45.740 --> 00:20:47.470
He finished the Synchro!

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:49.870
But Pendulum is also cool, right?

00:20:49.870 --> 00:20:52.490
Tanner, are you on Yuya's side?

00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:54.800
Crow takes care of us, you know!

00:20:54.800 --> 00:20:56.360
But still...

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:58.920
Layra, you're on Yuya's side, aren't you?

00:20:58.920 --> 00:21:00.770
Of course he is!

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:03.370
If Layra's on my side, I have the 
strength of a hundred guys!

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:08.550
L-Layra?

00:21:10.420 --> 00:21:12.600
Yeah, kids know the score!

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:14.650
Layra, you're on my side, right?

00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:18.920
Hey, now...

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:24.430
It's security! Run! We're surrounded!

00:21:24.730 --> 00:21:25.630
Surrounded?

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:27.330
Did they follow us here?

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:30.530
Oh, no!

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:41.160
Damn it...

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:49.320
Let go! Let go!

00:21:58.280 --> 00:21:59.560
L-Layra...

00:22:01.640 --> 00:22:03.870
Layra? Where's Layra?

00:22:04.220 --> 00:22:06.070
Keep your hands off those kids!

00:22:06.320 --> 00:22:07.540
Layra!

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:09.820
Layra!

00:23:45.940 --> 00:23:49.500
Welcome to the dead end for deadbeats.

00:23:49.930 --> 00:23:53.390
Starting today, this will be your happy home.

00:23:53.390 --> 00:23:54.810
We're confiscating your duel disks.

00:23:55.110 --> 00:23:57.700
We don't allow you to duel on your own here.

00:23:58.150 --> 00:24:00.060
You're returning our decks?

00:24:00.060 --> 00:24:03.290
In here, that's worth almost as much as your life.

00:24:03.290 --> 00:24:06.110
Well, take care of them.

00:24:06.920 --> 00:24:10.940
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
Even in Hell, Cards Determine Your Fate.

00:24:10.940 --> 00:24:12.900
The fun is only getting started!
